      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Imagine turning a simple "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "block",
            "ref": "v-block"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " of ice into a flower, a swan, or even a castle. This is the art of ice sculpting—where frozen water becomes a "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "canvas",
            "zh": "画布"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " for amazing artworks."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "But where did this idea come from? The history of using ice goes back thousands of years. In the "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Arctic",
            "zh": "北极"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", the Inuit people built snow houses long ago. In ancient China, farmers stored ice to keep food fresh. In Rome and India, rich people enjoyed drinks with ice."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Over time, people began carving ice into different shapes. In the 1600s, fishermen in Heilongjiang made ice lanterns by freezing water in "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "buckets",
            "zh": "桶"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " and placing candles inside. In 18th-century Russia, an "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "empress",
            "zh": "女皇"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " even ordered a palace made "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "entirely",
            "ref": "v-entirely"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " of ice."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Today, ice sculpting is often taught in cooking schools. It is closely related to fruit and vegetable carving. This tradition started long ago, when wealthy families used sugar and ice sculptures to decorate their meals."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Now, ice art is popular worldwide. There are many ice festivals, such as:"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "l1",
        "type": "list",
        "items": [
          [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "Harbin Ice Festival, China"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "Ice Magic Festival, Canada"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "Sapporo Snow Festival, Japan"
            }
          ]
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Ice sculpting has even been part of the Olympic cultural events, showing how this frozen art brings beauty and wonder to people everywhere."
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
